---
layout: data-page.njk
title: "Retained battles over time"
description: "Battles retained in Elixir's record, grouped by the UTC day they were played, with the daily mean and the busiest day."
permalink: /data/growth/index.html
canonical: /data/growth
dataNav: growth
---
{%- set bars = stats.series.battles_daily | dailyBars %}
<div class="page-head">
  <h1 class="hero-title" style="margin-bottom: 6px">Retained battles over time</h1>
  <p class="lede" style="margin: 0; max-width: 60ch">
    Battles currently in the record, grouped by the UTC day they were
    <em style="color: var(--ink-body)">played</em>.
  </p>
</div>

{% if not bars.bars %}
<section class="panel">
  <div class="panel__head"><span>Retained battles by played day</span></div>
  <div class="panel__body footnote">The chart is drawn from the daily series at build time; this build had no series to draw from.</div>
</section>
{% endif %}
{% if bars.bars %}
<section class="panel" style="margin-bottom: 22px">
  <div class="panel__head">
    <span>Retained battles by played day</span>
    <span class="footnote" style="border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 2px 8px; font-weight: 400">{{ bars.days }} days · UTC</span>
  </div>
  <div style="padding: 18px 18px 8px">
    {#- Bars, not a cumulative curve (2026-09-10): a running total only
        ever goes up and to the right, so a day the collectors stalled
        was invisible in it — and that is the day worth seeing. A day
        with no battles keeps its width as a real zero. -#}
    <svg viewBox="0 0 700 168" style="width: 100%; height: auto; display: block" role="img"
         aria-label="Retained battles by played day, {{ bars.first }} to {{ bars.last }}, peaking at {{ bars.top }} on {{ bars.busiest.day }}">
      <line x1="20" x2="640" y1="140" y2="140" stroke="var(--line)"></line>
      <line x1="20" x2="640" y1="76" y2="76" stroke="var(--line-soft)" stroke-dasharray="2 5"></line>
      <line x1="20" x2="640" y1="12" y2="12" stroke="var(--line-soft)" stroke-dasharray="2 5"></line>
      {%- for b in bars.bars %}
      <rect x="{{ b.x }}" y="{{ b.y }}" width="{{ b.width }}" height="{{ b.height }}" fill="var(--accent-bright)" opacity="0.85">
        <title>{{ b.day }} · {{ b.battles | number }} battles</title>
      </rect>
      {%- endfor %}
      <text x="648" y="16" fill="var(--ink-faint)" font-size="11" font-family="ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace">{{ bars.top | number }}</text>
      <text x="648" y="80" fill="var(--ink-faint)" font-size="11" font-family="ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace">{{ bars.half | number }}</text>
      {%- for tick in bars.ticks %}
      <text x="{{ tick.x }}" y="158" fill="var(--ink-faint)" font-size="11" font-family="ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace" text-anchor="middle">{{ tick.label }}</text>
      {%- endfor %}
    </svg>
  </div>
  <div class="panel__foot" style="font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-dim)">
    {{ bars.total | number }} retained battles in this {{ bars.days }}-day window, a mean of
    {{ bars.mean | number }} a day; the busiest was {{ bars.busiest.day }} with
    {{ bars.busiest.battles | number }}. The full retained record contains
    {{ stats.totals.battles | number }} battles across all dates.
    The newest day is partial.
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<p class="footnote" style="max-width: 78ch">
  Removed records are excluded.
  {% if stats.fetched_at %}Snapshot fetched {{ stats.fetched_at | stamp }};
  refreshed when this site is published. The source can be cached for up to an hour.{% endif %}
  Daily charts over the full history are in the
  <a href="/console/data/dashboard">console</a>.
</p>
